-- הוראת תכ"ם 13.4.2 "תשלום קצובת נסיעה", מהדורה 4 (17.5.2017)
-- The Accountant-General's instruction on the travel allowance of government
-- employees before the instruction was rewritten for the reform: the
-- cheapest tariff on the route, monthly free passes and single trips,
-- intercity travel by the days at the office within a cap of 1,330 shekels,
-- 1,660 in national-priority localities, the hourly employee, the blind
-- employee, a locality without public transport, the student, the
-- hard-roads post, Sabbath and holiday travel, who is not entitled,
-- reporting an address, income tax, and payment in "Malam" by annex B's
-- codes.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT `kitzuvat-nesia-common`
IMPORT `taarifei-nesia-common`
IMPORT `taarifei-nesia-in-force-common`

-- Tariffs: the notice "לוח תעריפי נסיעה בתחבורה ציבורית", `travel fares`, read off the notice in
-- force by `the travel allowance on the route` below. No rule here rounds (convention rounding.default).

-- not weighed against `the Hours of Work and Rest Law`: ‘יום עבודה בפועל’
-- here is the basis of a student's daily travel tariff (2.1.13), not the
-- hours of work and rest.

-- not weighed against `the Equal Pay Law`: ‘בעל’ here is the holder of a
-- post or of a service, personal or assigned car (‘בעל רכב צמוד’, ‘בעל תקן
-- דרכים קשות’), not a husband; the instruction sets one travel allowance
-- for every employee, man or woman, and does not distinguish between them.

§ `הוראת תכ"ם 13.4.2 תשלום קצובת נסיעה — מהדורה 4`

§§ `1 מבוא`

-- 1.1: the employees of the government ministries are entitled to the
-- travel allowance by public transport, on urban and intercity lines, set
-- for each category of employee and by their circumstances.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-1
GIVEN `employed by a government ministry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `edition 4 applies to` `employed by a government ministry` IF
    `employed by a government ministry`

-- akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-2 The instruction's purpose, to direct the accountancies and the employees on the travel allowance; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-3 A pointer to annex A, whose definitions the rules below cite; no rule.

§§ `2.1 זכאות לקצובת נסיעה`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1 The heading "זכאות לקצובת נסיעה"; its clauses follow.

-- 2.1.1 and annex A's definition 5: an employee who needs transport from
-- the residence to the workplace, by any means, is entitled to the travel
-- allowance (a refund of the actual expense) at the notice's rates and
-- terms; 2.3 takes out those who are not.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-1 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_5
GIVEN m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the travel allowance, edition 4` m IF
        m's `needs transport from home to work`
    AND NOT `not entitled under 2.3, edition 4` m

-- 2.1.2 and annex A's definition 3: from one residence only.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_3
`the residences the allowance is paid from, edition 4` MEANS 1

-- 2.1.3: at the cheapest public-transport tariff and the lowest price on
-- that route only.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-3
GIVEN `the prices on the route` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc the public-transport prices of the employee's route, from the notice
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the price the allowance is paid at, edition 4` `the prices on the route` IS
    minimum `the prices on the route`

-- 2.1.4: regardless of the frequency of transport and of when work starts
-- or ends.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-4
`the refund depends on the frequency of transport or the hours of work, edition 4` MEANS FALSE

-- 2.1.5-2.1.6: on lines where "חופשי חודשי" or "חופשי חודשי מרחבי"
-- applies, no more than the pass; on lines where neither applies, a single
-- trip there and back times the days the employee came to work, conditional
-- on the report and only for days at the permanent workplace.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-5 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-6
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the urban allowance, edition 4` f m IS
    IF m's `travels on lines with a monthly pass`
    THEN f's `monthly free pass`
    ELSE 2 TIMES f's `single fare` TIMES m's `days actually worked`

-- 2.1.7-2.1.8: an employee who needs the monthly pass and intercity travel
-- too is paid both; individual intercity travel is paid for the days the
-- employee came to the office only (2.1.8), only where the days are
-- reported in the payroll (2.1.8.1), at a single fare there and back, and
-- the whole within 1,330 shekels a month (2.1.7, 2.1.8.3).
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-7 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-8 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-8__pnt_2-1-8-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-8__pnt_2-1-8-3
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`, `the days are reported in the payroll` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the intercity allowance, edition 4` f m `the days are reported in the payroll` IS
    IF m's `travels intercity individually` AND `the days are reported in the payroll`
    THEN 2 TIMES f's `intercity single fare` TIMES m's `days actually worked`
    ELSE 0

-- 2.1.8.2: no lump-sum intercity allowance is approved.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-8__pnt_2-1-8-2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel-allowance duty`
DECIDE `no lump-sum intercity allowance, edition 4` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    SHANT `pay a lump-sum intercity allowance`

-- 2.1.9.1-2.1.9.2: an employee living in a national-priority locality (the
-- takshir's chapter 28.3) is paid the monthly pass and the intercity trips
-- up to 1,660 shekels a month, and the allowances of every kind together
-- no more. Everyone else, 1,330 (2.1.7, 2.1.8.3, annex B §4).
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-9 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-9__pnt_2-1-9-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-9__pnt_2-1-9-2 akn:att_2__hc_1__para_5
GIVEN m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly cap, edition 4` m IS
    IF m's `lives in a national-priority locality` THEN 1660 ELSE 1330

-- 2.1.9.3: an employee carried part of the month by a government vehicle or
-- another Treasury-funded arrangement is paid in proportion. Printed under
-- 2.1.9, the national-priority localities, it is read as that clause's
-- (convention reading.placement); edition 5 moves it among the general
-- clauses (its 2.4.4).
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-9__pnt_2-1-9-3
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the partial allowance in a national-priority locality, edition 4` amount m IS
    IF m's `lives in a national-priority locality`
    THEN `in proportion to the trips not State-funded` amount m
    ELSE amount

-- 2.1.10: the hourly employee, single trips for the days travelled to work
-- (there and back, as 2.1.6 counts a day), no more than the monthly pass.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-10 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-10__pnt_2-1-10-1
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the hourly employee's allowance, edition 4` f m IS
    min (2 TIMES f's `single fare` TIMES m's `days actually worked`) (f's `monthly free pass`)

-- 2.1.11 and annex A's definition 4: a blind employee is paid five monthly
-- passes, an entitlement that cancels every other. Annex B §4 caps every
-- travel code at 1,330 "in no case" more, the blind employee's 0971 among
-- them (F-2017-05-17_takam_H-13-4-2_kitzuvat-nesia_v4-a). The reading
-- adopted (convention precedence.specific): the blind employee's own rule
-- prevails, not capped.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-11 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-11__pnt_2-1-11-1 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the blind employee's allowance, edition 4` f IS
    5 TIMES f's `monthly free pass`

-- 2.1.12: an employee living in a locality without public transport, who
-- uses another means to reach the main road on the way to work, is entitled
-- to a monthly pass of 128 shekels for those trips (code 901).
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-12 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-12__pnt_2-1-12-1
GIVEN m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the pass for a locality without public transport, edition 4` m IS
    IF m's `lives where there is no public transport` THEN 128 ELSE 0

-- 2.1.13: a student employee is paid by law and the collective agreement
-- in force for each day actually worked, or the monthly pass, whichever is
-- lower. The day's amount is the law's and the agreement's: an input.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-13 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-13__pnt_2-1-13-1
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`, `the student's day by law and agreement` IS A NUMBER @desc the travel allowance for a day actually worked that the law and the collective agreement in force give a student
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the student's allowance, edition 4` f m `the student's day by law and agreement` IS
    min (`the student's day by law and agreement` TIMES m's `days actually worked`) (f's `monthly free pass`)

-- 2.1.14 and annex A's definition 1 (hard roads: unpaved roads): an
-- employee with a hard-roads post is paid the monthly or regional monthly
-- pass, never a refund by the kilometre (2.1.14.1); no deduction is made in
-- proportion to the days worked, save the cases 2.1.14.2 names "in section
-- 2.2.3", which pays the Sabbath; the absence of a month that 2.3.3
-- excludes is read (F-2017-05-17_takam_H-13-4-2_kitzuvat-nesia_v4-b).
-- Intercity trips are paid by the reported days at the office (2.1.14.3).
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-14 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-14__pnt_2-1-14-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-14__pnt_2-1-14-2 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-14__pnt_2-1-14-3 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_1
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the hard-roads allowance, edition 4` f m IS
    f's `monthly free pass`

`a hard-roads allowance is refunded by the kilometre, edition 4` MEANS FALSE

-- The allowance for the way to work, by the kind of employee.
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`, `the student's day by law and agreement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the allowance for travel to work, edition 4` f m `the student's day by law and agreement` IS
    CONSIDER m's `kind of employee`
    WHEN `an employee paid by the hour` THEN `the hourly employee's allowance, edition 4` f m
    WHEN `a student employee` THEN `the student's allowance, edition 4` f m `the student's day by law and agreement`
    WHEN `an employee with a hard-roads post` THEN `the hard-roads allowance, edition 4` f m
    OTHERWISE `the urban allowance, edition 4` f m

§§ `2.2 תשלום קצובת נסיעה בגין נסיעות בשבתות וחגים`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2 The heading; its clauses follow.
-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-2 The heading "תנאי הזכאות"; its condition follows.
-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-3 The heading "אופן התשלום"; its clauses follow.

-- 2.2.1-2.2.3: an employee employed on the Sabbath or a holiday who starts
-- work after it has come in, with no public transport, is paid double the
-- cost of an individual public-transport trip from home to work and back,
-- only for the days the employee actually came. Not for an employee with a
-- service or personal car, nor in an office with a shuttle. 2.2.3.1 sends
-- to "section 4.2.1 above", which the edition does not have; the condition
-- of 2.2.2.1 is read (F-2017-05-17_takam_H-13-4-2_kitzuvat-nesia_v4-b).
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-2__pnt_2-2-2-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-3__pnt_2-2-3-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-3__pnt_2-2-3-2
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the Sabbath and holiday allowance, edition 4` f m IS
    IF m's `has a service or personal car` OR m's `the office runs a shuttle`
    THEN 0
    ELSE 2 TIMES (2 TIMES f's `single fare`) TIMES m's `Sabbath and holiday days reached`

-- 2.2.4 and annex B §4: the Sabbath refund and the monthly allowance, and
-- every travel code, within the cap. 2.2.4 sends the cap to the notice,
-- which prints none; the edition's own cap is read
-- (F-2017-05-17_takam_H-13-4-2_kitzuvat-nesia_v4-b). The month's travel
-- allowance: none where 2.3 takes the employee out; the blind employee's in
-- place of every other; otherwise everything within the cap.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-4 akn:att_2__hc_1__para_4
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`, `the days are reported in the payroll` IS A BOOLEAN, `the student's day by law and agreement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the travel allowance, edition 4` f m `the days are reported in the payroll` `the student's day by law and agreement` IS
    BRANCH IF NOT `entitled to the travel allowance, edition 4` m THEN 0
           IF m's `blind` THEN `the blind employee's allowance, edition 4` f
           OTHERWISE min (`the partial allowance in a national-priority locality, edition 4`
                              (     `the allowance for travel to work, edition 4` f m `the student's day by law and agreement`
                               PLUS `the intercity allowance, edition 4` f m `the days are reported in the payroll`
                               PLUS `the Sabbath and holiday allowance, edition 4` f m
                               PLUS `the pass for a locality without public transport, edition 4` m)
                              m)
                         (`the monthly cap, edition 4` m)

-- Annex B §4 against 2.1.9 and 2.1.11: "in no case" more than 1,330, where
-- a priority-area resident may be paid 1,660 and a blind employee five
-- monthly passes.
@ref akn:att_2__hc_1__para_4
`the cap annex B §4 puts on every code, edition 4` MEANS 1330

`annex B §4 caps below what 2.1.9 and 2.1.11 pay, edition 4` MEANS
        `the cap annex B §4 puts on every code, edition 4` LESS THAN 1660
    AND `the cap annex B §4 puts on every code, edition 4` LESS THAN 5 TIMES 300
#ASSERT `annex B §4 caps below what 2.1.9 and 2.1.11 pay, edition 4`

-- The section numbers the edition prints against those its cross-references
-- send to: 2.2.3.1's "4.2.1" and annex B's "4.1.8" are not among them.
`the clauses edition 4 numbers` MEANS
    LIST "2.1.8", "2.1.14", "2.2.2.1", "2.2.3", "2.3.3"

`edition 4 cites clauses it does not have` MEANS
        NOT elem "4.2.1" `the clauses edition 4 numbers`
    AND NOT elem "4.1.8" `the clauses edition 4 numbers`
#ASSERT `edition 4 cites clauses it does not have`

§§ `2.3 אי זכאות לקצובת נסיעה`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3 The heading; its clauses follow.

-- 2.3.1-2.3.3 and annex A's definition 2 (a calendar month): not entitled
-- is an employee carried to or from work by a government vehicle or another
-- Treasury-funded arrangement, one with an assigned car, and, for that
-- period, one absent an unbroken calendar month or more.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-2 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-3 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_2
GIVEN m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `not entitled under 2.3, edition 4` m IF
        m's `share of trips by a State-funded arrangement` AT LEAST 1
    OR  m's `has an assigned car`
    OR  m's `absent a calendar month or more`

§§ `2.4 דיווח על כתובת מגורים`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-4 The heading; its clauses follow.

-- 2.4.1-2.4.2: an employee who changed residence or workplace reports it to
-- the office's administration on the form "קצובת נסיעה"; the
-- administration passes it to the salary unit, and the employee is paid by
-- the new lines. One who does not report the new lines is not paid (the
-- payroll blocks it) until the update is made.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-4__cls_2-4-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-4__cls_2-4-2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel-allowance duty`
DECIDE `reporting a move, edition 4` IS
    PARTY `the government employee`
    MUST  `report the new address or workplace on the travel-allowance form`
    HENCE (PARTY `the employer`
           MUST  `pass the report to the salary unit`
           HENCE (PARTY `the employer`
                  MUST  `pay the updated travel allowance`))
    LEST  (PARTY `the employer`
           MAY   `block the travel allowance in the payroll`)

-- 2.4.3: the employee refreshes the details at least once in 3 years; the
-- payment is blocked until it is done. Months.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-4__cls_2-4-3
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel-allowance duty`
DECIDE `refreshing the details, edition 4` IS
    PARTY `the government employee`
    MUST  `refresh the travel-allowance details`
    WITHIN 36
    LEST  (PARTY `the employer`
           MAY   `block the travel allowance in the payroll`)

§§ `2.5 ניכוי מס הכנסה`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-5 The heading; its clauses follow.

-- 2.5.1: income tax is deducted as the notice "ניכוי מס הכנסה" sets out;
-- the corpus does not hold it.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-5__cls_2-5-1
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel-allowance duty`
DECIDE `withholding income tax, edition 4` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `withhold income tax from the travel allowance`

-- 2.5.2: the tax is grossed up on the amounts above those the notice
-- names, and for an employee in a national-priority locality (the
-- takshir's chapter 28.37) likewise; the notice's amount is an input.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-5__cls_2-5-2
GIVEN allowance IS A NUMBER, `the amount the tax notice names` IS A NUMBER @desc the amount above which the notice "ניכוי מס הכנסה" has the tax grossed up
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel-allowance duty`
DECIDE `grossing up the tax, edition 4` allowance `the amount the tax notice names` IS
    IF `the part above` allowance `the amount the tax notice names` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `gross up the tax on the travel allowance` `part`
               PROVIDED `part` EQUALS `the part above` allowance `the amount the tax notice names`
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `2.6 תשלום קצובת הנסיעה`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-6 The heading; its clauses follow.
-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-6__cls_2-6-2 The heading "payment not through Malam"; its clause follows.

-- 2.6.1 and annex B §1: paid through "Malam" by the instruction and annex
-- B's codes. 2.6.2.1 and annex B §6: an accountancy whose salaries are not
-- prepared in "Malam" pays by the instruction's rules.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-6__cls_2-6-1 akn:att_2__hc_1__para_1
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel-allowance duty`
DECIDE `paying through the payroll, edition 4` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the travel allowance through the payroll`

@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-6__cls_2-6-2__pnt_2-6-2-1 akn:att_2__hc_1__para_6
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel-allowance duty`
DECIDE `paying outside Malam, edition 4` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the travel allowance by the instruction's rules outside Malam`

§§ `3-4 מסמכים ישימים ונספחים`

-- akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-1 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-2 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-3 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-4 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-5 The applicable documents (the takshir's chapters 28.3 and 28.37, the form, two notices); a source list, no rule.
-- akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-1 akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-2 akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-3 The list of annexes; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p1 Annex A's title "הגדרות"; its definitions are cited by the rules that use them.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1/p1 Annex B's title; its clauses follow.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1__para_2 akn:att_2__hc_1__para_2/t1 The "Malam" code each kind of payment is paid under (0614, 0604, event 226 code 4820 "(סעיף 4.1.8)", 0971 for the blind employee's code 99 times 5, 901, 0960); payroll coding, no entitlement of its own (its stale "4.1.8" is F-2017-05-17_takam_H-13-4-2_kitzuvat-nesia_v4-b's).
-- akn:att_2__hc_1__para_3 The codes of the public-transport lines are the notice's; a pointer, no rule.
-- akn:att_3__hc_1/p1 akn:att_3__hc_1/p2 akn:att_3__hc_1/t1 Annex C, the table of the editions' changes; a record, no rule.

§§ `התעריפים — the notice in force`

-- The edition reads the monthly free pass and the single fare, the intercity single fare; here they are read off the notice
-- "לוח תעריפי נסיעה בתחבורה ציבורית" in force on the month's day (HOD
-- 13.4.2.1, `taarifei-nesia-in-force-common`), for the employee's route. Where
-- the notice prints no tariff the edition reads, there is no answer.
GIVEN r IS A `travel route`, d IS A DATE @desc the month's day
      m IS A `travel month`
      `the days are reported in the payroll` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the student's day by law and agreement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the travel allowance on the route, edition 4` r d m `the days are reported in the payroll` `the student's day by law and agreement` IS
    CONSIDER `the travel fares of the route on` r d FALSE TRUE TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST f THEN JUST (`the travel allowance, edition 4` f m `the days are reported in the payroll` `the student's day by law and agreement`)

§§ `Worked examples`

`placeholder fares, edition 4` MEANS
    `travel fares` WITH
        `monthly free pass`     IS 300
        `daily free pass`       IS 0
        `single fare`           IS 8
        `intercity single fare` IS 20

`edition 4 pays` m MEANS `the travel allowance, edition 4` `placeholder fares, edition 4` m TRUE 12

#ASSERT `edition 4 pays` (`an ordinary travel month` `a monthly employee` 22) EQUALS 300

-- 2.1.7-2.1.8: the monthly pass and 22 days of intercity trips there and
-- back at 20 (880), within 1,330.
`an intercity month, edition 4` MEANS
    `the travel month changed` (`an ordinary travel month` `a monthly employee` 22) TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE 0 0
#ASSERT `edition 4 pays` `an intercity month, edition 4` EQUALS 1180

-- 2.1.8.3 and 2.2.4: with six Sabbath days (6 x 2 x 2 x 8 = 192) the month
-- passes the cap.
`an intercity month with Sabbaths, edition 4` MEANS
    `the travel month changed` (`an ordinary travel month` `a monthly employee` 22) TRUE FALSE 6 FALSE TRUE 0 0
#ASSERT `edition 4 pays` `an intercity month with Sabbaths, edition 4` EQUALS 1330

-- 2.1.10 and 2.1.13: an hourly employee of 10 days (160) and a student of
-- 10 days at 12 a day (120).
#ASSERT `edition 4 pays` (`an ordinary travel month` `an employee paid by the hour` 10) EQUALS 160
#ASSERT `edition 4 pays` (`an ordinary travel month` `a student employee` 10) EQUALS 120

-- 2.1.11 as read: five monthly passes, not capped.
`a blind employee's month, edition 4` MEANS
    `the travel month changed` (`an ordinary travel month` `a monthly employee` 22) TRUE TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0
#ASSERT `edition 4 pays` `a blind employee's month, edition 4` EQUALS 1500

-- On 1.6.2017, a monthly employee of 22 days on `a 30 km route` (the
-- Tel Aviv codes before the reform, 30 km by bus after it): the edition's
-- allowance on the tariffs the notice in force prints.
#ASSERT `the travel allowance on the route, edition 4` `a 30 km route` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2017) (`an ordinary travel month` `a monthly employee` 22) TRUE 12 EQUALS
    JUST (`the travel allowance, edition 4` `the route's fares on 1.6.2017, edition 4` (`an ordinary travel month` `a monthly employee` 22) TRUE 12)

`the route's fares on 1.6.2017, edition 4` MEANS
    `travel fares` WITH
        `monthly free pass`     IS 213
        `daily free pass`       IS 0
        `single fare`           IS 2.3
        `intercity single fare` IS 5
